*> IC116M -- "CALL without the optional USING phrase" from the NIST
*> COBOL-85 suite. IC116M is the driving main program; it CALLs the
*> subprogram IC117M (which in turn CALLs IC118M).
*>
*> USNG-TEST-01 is the paragraph that issues `CALL "IC117M"`. Driving it
*> on its own keeps the run away from the CCVS print-file machinery, so the
*> single mocked CALL is the only boundary that needs standing in.
TESTSUITE "IC116M CALL without USING phrase"

TESTCASE "USNG-TEST-01 calls subprogram IC117M (mocked)"
    MOCK CALL "IC117M"
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM USNG-TEST-01
    VERIFY CALL "IC117M" WAS CALLED ONCE
